Copy the fields under Find and Replace exactly as is (excluding the Find: and Replace: parts)

Headers:

First, we need to add special headers to the XML file for proper data formatting. 

Find: 
xmlns:mods="http://www.loc.gov/mods/v3"

Replace: 
xmlns:mods="http://www.loc.gov/mods/v3" xmlns:rts="https://www.loc.gov/standards/rights/METSRights.xsd" xmlns:textMD="https://www.loc.gov/standards/textMD/"

Admin and TechMD:

This time, we need to add metadata for file creation, formatting, and administration. 

Find: 
</METS:dmdSec>

Replace: 
</METS:dmdSec><METS:amdSec><METS:techMD><METS:mdWrap MDTYPE="PDF"><METS:xmlData></METS:xmlData></METS:mdWrap></METS:techMD><METS:rightsMD ID="ADMD"><METS:mdWrap MDTYPE="other" OTHERMDTYPE="METSRights"><METS:xmlData><rts:RightsDeclaration MDRIGHTSCATEGORY="Public Domain"><rts:Context CONTEXTCLASS="General Public"><rts:ConstraintDescription>Public Domain</rts:ConstraintDescription></rts:Context></rts:RightsDeclaration></METS:xmlData></METS:mdWrap></METS:rightsMD><METS:digiProvMD><METS:xmlData><textMD:textMD><textMD:encoding><textMD:encoding_platform>Windows 10</textMD:encoding_platform><textMD:encoding_software>Opus FreeFlow</textMD:encoding_software><textMD:encoding_software>SobekCM</textMD:encoding_software><textMD:encoding_software>MarcEdit 7</textMD:encoding_software><textMD:encoding_agent>Erin Fernandes</textMD:encoding_agent><textMD:encoding_agent>Allison Tyous</textMD:encoding_agent></textMD:encoding><textMD:pageOrder>Left-to-right</textMD:pageOrder><textMD:representationSequence>Reading-order</textMD:representationSequence><textMD:lineOrientation>Horizontal</textMD:lineOrientation><textMD:lineLayout>Top-to-bottom</textMD:lineLayout><textMD:characterFlow>Left-to-right</textMD:characterFlow></textMD:textMD></METS:xmlData></METS:digiProvMD></METS:amdSec>

Identifier:

We need to add information to the identifier fields to explain what they are identifying.

Find: <mods:identifier>

Replace (for Koha numbers): 
<mods:identifier type="koha">

Replace (for Public Law numbers):
<mods:identifier type="public law">

Changing Extent to Form:

SobekCM automatically fills out some fields differently from the GPO's guidelines. This helps switch the fields to match the GPO's guidelines for MODS metadata.

Find: 
<mods:extent>txt--rdacontent; computer--rdamedia; computer file--rdacarrier; text file--rdaft--PDF</mods:extent>

Replace: 
<mods:form type="digital">txt--rdacontent; computer--rdamedia; computer file--rdacarrier; text file--rdaft--PDF</mods:form>

Specifying the URL Type:

Find: 
<mods:url displayLabel="Related URL">

Replace: 
<mods:url displayLabel="Content Detail">

Page numbers: 

I use the extent to explain page numbers - it can help with ensuring you've selected hte right document.

Find:
<mods:physicalDescription>

Replace:
<mods:physicalDescription><mods:extent unit="pages">xxxxx</mods:extent>

Batch deletions:

Finally, while I recommend doing MARC-related batch edits in Excel, you can do so in this step if you forgot to do it in Excel.

Find (enter one of the following, minus brackets but including the spaces): 
[ $2 ], $b, $c, $d, $e, $t, $x, $v, $z

Replace:
[ ] (in other words, press the space bar once)

There are metadata fields that are manually edited, depending on the document or document type (easy example: number of pages). This handles the batch edits, however.
